sentences.l:
it is good also to obey night,
so that you may gladden all the Achaeans beside the ships,
and most of all your own kinsmen and companions, those who are yours;

and they were glad,
when they saw him both alive and unharmed, coming near,
having escaped the might of Ajax and his hands, untouchable;

And when they had come to be in the huts of Atreus’-son,
for them an ox sacrificed the lord of men, Agamemnon,
a male, five-year-old, to the exceeding-strong son of Cronus.

But when of drink and of food they had put away desire,
for them the old man, first of all, began to weave a plan,
Nestor, whose counsel earlier too appeared best;

therefore you must with dawn stop the war of the Achaeans,
and let us ourselves, gathered together, wheel the dead to here
with oxen and with mules;

and at dawn let Idaeus go to the hollow ships
to tell the sons of Atreus, Agamemnon and Menelaus,
the word of Alexander, for whose sake the quarrel has arisen;
